* Declaration of Sentiments from 1st Women's Rights Convention in the U.S.

It was held in Seneca Falls, New York, the nineteenth and twentieth of
July, 1848. Among the famous who signed are Elizabeth Cady Stanton,
whose home in Seneca Falls is now part of the Women's Rights National
Park, and Frederick Douglass.

